<!--{ er02 : rich }-->
# 9. Errors

A formula that cannot be computed shows **[[Undefined]]**, highlighted, and
the rest of the document still works. This lesson has two such errors on
purpose. You find them and fix them. About four minutes.
<!--{ er03 : markdown }-->
A beam of span <% L = 6, q = "12.5" %>**L = <% L %> m** carries a load of
**q = <% q %> kN/m**.
<!--{ er04 : markdown }-->
The midspan moment is **<% moment: q * L ^ 2 / 8 %> kNm**, and the
utilisation of the section is **<% u: moment / 80 %>**.
<!--{ er05 : rich }-->
## Find them

The editor shows you where each error is:

- The value is **highlighted** in its line. Point at it to read the reason.
- The **right margin** shows a warning icon, with the number of errors on
  that line.
- The **warning button** in the top bar shows the total of the document.

Click the warning button: the **Errors** pane opens on the right and lists
each error, with what went wrong, the formula, and the line. Under
**Caused by** it lists the earlier errors that led to this one: the last one
is the origin. Fix that one, and the others follow.
<!--{ er06 : rich }-->
## Fix them

The origin is the load: `"12.5"` is written between double quotes, so it is
a text, and a text cannot be multiplied. Edit the line with the span and the
load, remove the quotes around `12.5`, and press **Ctrl+Enter**. Both errors
go away.
<!--{ er07 : formula }-->
<% tutorial.check (moment == 56.25) %>
<!--{ er08 : markdown }-->
## A misspelled name is not an error

A name that is misspelled, or used before it is given, shows nothing at all:
here is <% Moment %> a misspelled `Moment`, between "is" and "a". It is not
listed as an error, so when a value is missing, check its name.

Only a value that a formula *shows* is an error: a value that is only given
a name, or that sits inside a list, is not counted until a formula shows it.

More in the manual: [Errors](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/errors.html).
<!--{ er09 : rich }-->
